    questionText: "Calculate the U-value of the floor, given the construction has the following sequence and data: Hardwood flooring thickness 20 mm; sand/cement fine screed thickness 65 mm; floor insulation thickness 200mm; concrete floor slab thickness 150 mm; radon barrier thickness 0.25 mm; sand blinding thickness 40 mm; hardcore thickness 200 mm; subsoil thickness 300 mm. Thermal data of the ground floor: resistance of internal top surface of floor (R) 0.104 m2 ⁰C/W; conductivity of hardwood flooring (k) 6.666 W/m ⁰C; resistivity of fine screed (r) 1.410 m ⁰C/W; conductivity of floor insulation (k) 0.022 W/m ⁰C; conductivity of concrete floor slab (k) 1.280 W/m ⁰C; conductivity of radon barrier (k) 0.250 W/m ⁰C; conductivity of sand blinding (k) 0.160 W/m ⁰C; conductivity of hardcore (k) 1.350 W/m ⁰C; conductivity of subsoil (k) 1.600 W/m ⁰C.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 33,
    rows: [
    { id: "resistances", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Formulae: R=T/k R=T × r", marks: 27, contextNote: "Nine resistances, 3 each, by R = T/k (or R = T × r for the screed): internal surface 0.104 (given); hardwood 0.02/6.666 = 0.003; screed 0.065 × 1.410 = 0.092; insulation 0.2/0.022 = 9.091; slab 0.15/1.28 = 0.117; radon barrier 0.00025/0.25 = 0.001; sand blinding 0.04/0.16 = 0.25; hardcore 0.2/1.35 = 0.148; subsoil 0.3/1.6 = 0.188. All in m²°C/W.", permittedMarks: [0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,27] },
    { id: "total-resistance", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Total resistance (R)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Total resistance Rt = 9.993 m²°C/W.", permittedMarks: [0,3] },
    { id: "u-value", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Calculation of U- value", marks: 3, contextNote: "U = 1 ÷ Rt = 1 ÷ 9.993 = 0.10 W/m²°C, with units.", permittedMarks: [0,3] },
    ],
