    stem: "The sketch shows the proposed design of a Passive House which is to be constructed in a rural setting.",
    questionText: "Using notes and freehand sketches, discuss the importance of any two of the following in Passive House design: building form; foundation design; space heating energy demand.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 20,
    rows: [
    { id: "items", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Discuss the importance of any two in Passive House design", marks: 20, contextNote: "Any two of the three, each notes 5 and sketches 5 = 10. Building form: a compact, simple rectangular form with the smallest surface area (A/V ratio 0.7 or less) to cut heat loss, materials and cost; a narrow plan, one room deep, to maximise solar gain; clean lines in walls and roof that make airtightness easy. Foundation design: insulated ring-beam or passive raft foundations wrapped in insulation to eliminate thermal bridging; thermal blocks in the inner-leaf rising wall; 50–100 mm edge insulation at the floor/wall junction; thermally broken wall ties; a U-value of 0.10–0.15 W/m²K. Space heating energy demand: passive house space-heating demand of no more than 15 kWh/m² per year; quality workmanship in airtightness and insulation; eliminating thermal bridges; solar gain through well-designed fenestration; solar shading, thermal mass and controlled ventilation to keep about 20 °C all year.", group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":10,"options":["Building form","Foundation design","Space heating energy demand"]} },
    ],
