    id: "cons-2022-hl-q4-complete", topicId: "cons-2-2", conceptId: "foundation-design-complete",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q4 — complete",
    questionText: "(a) Discuss in detail, using notes and freehand sketches, three functional requirements of a foundation suitable for a dwelling house. (b) The owners of the site shown have been granted permission to construct a two-storey house. Site investigations have revealed moderately firm clay subsoil for the foundations. The external wall of the house is to be a 450 mm concrete block wall with a full-fill insulated cavity. Using notes and freehand sketches, show the typical design detailing for two different foundations suitable for the proposed house. Indicate the position of the reinforcement and the typical dimensions of each foundation. (c) Discuss one advantage and one disadvantage of each foundation you have shown at 4(b) above.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 60,
    rows: [
    { id: "a-requirement-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Functional requirement 1", marks: 8, contextNote: "Notes 4 and sketches 4. Such as: to distribute all live loads (wind, snow, furniture, people) and dead loads (the building’s own weight) evenly to the ground.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] },
    { id: "a-requirement-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Functional requirement 2", marks: 8, contextNote: "A second, different requirement: notes 4 and sketches 4. Such as: to anchor the building against wind; to give a level surface to build on; to limit differential settlement.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] },
    { id: "a-requirement-3", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Functional requirement 3", marks: 8, contextNote: "A third, different requirement: notes 4 and sketches 4. Such as: to resist failure under applied stresses; to withstand swelling or shrinking of the surrounding soil; to give the building stability.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] },
    { id: "b-foundation-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Foundation design 1", marks: 8, contextNote: "Notes 4 and sketches 4 for one foundation. Such as, a strip foundation for a 450 mm wall (T): depth T, width 3T = 1350 mm, projecting T beyond the wall; its top at least 600 mm below ground, on firm subsoil about 1000 mm down.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] },
    { id: "b-details-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Reinforcement (2) + dimensions (2)", marks: 4, contextNote: "Reinforcement 2 and dimensions 2 for the first foundation. Such as: 10 mm welded steel mesh and longitudinal bars with 80 mm cover; the dimensions above.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4], parts: [{"id":"reinforcement","verbatim":"Reinforcement","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]},{"id":"dimensions","verbatim":"dimensions","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    { id: "b-foundation-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Foundation design 2", marks: 8, contextNote: "Notes 4 and sketches 4 for a second, different foundation. Such as, a passive insulated raft: rigid EPS edge formwork carrying the 450 mm wall, 300 mm of EPS under a 100–150 mm reinforced slab, on compacted hardcore, blinding and a radon membrane.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8] },
    { id: "b-details-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Reinforcement (2) + dimensions (2)", marks: 4, contextNote: "Reinforcement 2 and dimensions 2 for the second foundation. Such as: steel in the edge beam tied to 10 mm mesh at 200 mm centres raised on spacers; the dimensions above.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4], parts: [{"id":"reinforcement","verbatim":"Reinforcement","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]},{"id":"dimensions","verbatim":"dimensions","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    { id: "c-advantage-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Foundation design 1 Advantage (1 for point, 2 for discussion)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Point 1 and discussion 2. Such as, strip: well understood, shallow, cheap and quick to build.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3], parts: [{"id":"point","verbatim":"point","marks":1,"permittedMarks":[0,1]},{"id":"discussion","verbatim":"discussion","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    { id: "c-disadvantage-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Disadvantage (1 for point, 2 for discussion)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Point 1 and discussion 2. Such as, strip: a large volume of concrete with high embodied energy; uninsulated, so heat is lost; limited to medium bearing soils and buildings.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3], parts: [{"id":"point","verbatim":"point","marks":1,"permittedMarks":[0,1]},{"id":"discussion","verbatim":"discussion","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    { id: "c-advantage-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Foundation design 2 Advantage (1 for point, 2 for discussion)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Point 1 and discussion 2 for the second foundation. Such as, insulated raft: minimal excavation; less concrete and embodied energy; very quick; no thermal bridge at the wall-floor junction.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3], parts: [{"id":"point","verbatim":"point","marks":1,"permittedMarks":[0,1]},{"id":"discussion","verbatim":"discussion","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    { id: "c-disadvantage-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Disadvantage (1 for point, 2 for discussion)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Point 1 and discussion 2 for the second foundation. Such as, insulated raft: high workmanship and specialist training; an engineer’s design for each house; higher capital cost.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3], parts: [{"id":"point","verbatim":"point","marks":1,"permittedMarks":[0,1]},{"id":"discussion","verbatim":"discussion","marks":2,"permittedMarks":[0,1,2]}] },
    ],
