    section: "B", questionRef: "2019 HL Q5 — complete",
    stem: "The external wall of a house built in the 1990s is of 100 mm concrete block construction with a 100 mm partially filled cavity, as shown.",
    questionText: "(a) Calculate the U-value of the wall, given the construction has the following sequence and data: External render thickness 16 mm; Concrete block outer leaf thickness 100 mm; Clear cavity width 50 mm; Polystyrene insulation thickness 50 mm; Concrete block inner leaf thickness 100 mm; Internal plaster thickness 12 mm. Thermal data of the external wall: Resistance of external surface (R) 0.048 m2 °C/W; Resistivity of external render (r) 2.170 m °C/W; Conductivity of concrete external blockwork (k) 1.440 W/m °C; Resistance of clear cavity (R) 0.170 m2 °C/W; Conductivity of insulation (k) 0.037 W/m °C; Conductivity of concrete internal blockwork (k) 1.440 W/m °C; Resistivity of internal plaster (r) 6.250 m °C/W; Resistance of internal surface (R) 0.122 m2 °C/W. (b) Using the U-value of the wall obtained at 5(a) above and the following data, calculate the cost of heat lost annually through this wall: area of external wall 135 m2; average internal temperature 19 °C; average external temperature 5 °C; heating period 9 hours daily for 36 weeks per annum; cost of oil 94 cent per litre; calorific value of oil 37350 kJ per litre; 1000 Watts 1 kJ per second. (c) It is proposed to upgrade the thermal properties of the above wall, to meet the Passive House standard, by fixing expanded polystyrene to the external surface, as shown. Given the thermal conductivity (k) of expanded polystyrene as 0.031 W/m°C, calculate the thickness of expanded polystyrene required to achieve a U-value of 0.15 W/m2 °C.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 60,
    rows: [
    { id: "a-resistances", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Formulae: R=T/k R=T × r", marks: 24, contextNote: "Eight resistances, 3 each, by R = T/k (or R = T × r for render and plaster): external surface 0.048 (given); render 0.016 × 2.170 = 0.035; external blockwork 0.1/1.44 = 0.069; clear cavity 0.170 (given); insulation 0.05/0.037 = 1.351; internal blockwork 0.1/1.44 = 0.069; plaster 0.012 × 6.25 = 0.075; internal surface 0.122 (given). All in m²°C/W.", permittedMarks: [0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24] },
    { id: "a-total-resistance", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Total resistance", marks: 3, contextNote: "Total resistance Rt = 1.939 m²°C/W.", permittedMarks: [0,3] },
    { id: "a-u-value", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Calculation of U- value", marks: 3, contextNote: "U = 1 ÷ Rt = 1 ÷ 1.939 = 0.516 W/m²°C, with units.", permittedMarks: [0,3] },
    { id: "b-heat-loss", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Heat loss formula and calculations", marks: 3, contextNote: "Heat loss = U-value × area × temperature difference = 0.516 × 135 × (19 − 5) = 975.24 watts (joules per second).", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "b-duration", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Heating duration for one year", marks: 3, contextNote: "Heating period = 60 × 60 × 9 × 7 × 36 = 8,164,800 seconds (2,268 hours).", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "b-energy", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "k/Joules calculation for one year", marks: 3, contextNote: "Energy = 8,164,800 × 975.24 ÷ 1000 = 7,962,639.552 kJ per year.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "b-oil", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Litres of oil for one year", marks: 3, contextNote: "Oil = 7,962,639.552 ÷ 37,350 = 212.34 litres per year.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "b-cost", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Annual cost of heat loss", marks: 3, contextNote: "Annual cost = 212.34 × €0.94 = €199.60. The scheme’s alternative one-line method gives the same €199.60.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "c-required-resistance", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Resistance for U- value for 0.15Wm2K (using R=1/U)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Required resistance = 1 ÷ 0.15 = 6.666 m²K/W.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "c-existing-resistance", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Resistance from calculated U-value from part (a)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Existing resistance = 1 ÷ 0.516 = 1.939 m²K/W (the scheme prints the divisor as 0.156).", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "c-difference", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Difference in resistances (required resistance)", marks: 3, contextNote: "Difference = 6.666 − 1.939 = 4.727 m²K/W.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "c-formula", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Application of formula R = T/k", marks: 3, contextNote: "R = T/k, so 4.727 = T/0.031.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "c-thickness", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Required thickness of insulation", marks: 3, contextNote: "T = 4.727 × 0.031 = 0.146537 m: 147 mm of expanded polystyrene (146 or 147 mm accepted).", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    ],
    taskGroups: [{"sourceCardId":"cons-2019-hl-q5-a","label":"a","marks":30,"rowIds":["a-resistances","a-total-resistance","a-u-value"]},{"sourceCardId":"cons-2019-hl-q5-b","label":"b","marks":15,"rowIds":["b-heat-loss","b-duration","b-energy","b-oil","b-cost"]},{"sourceCardId":"cons-2019-hl-q5-c","label":"c","marks":15,"rowIds":["c-required-resistance","c-existing-resistance","c-difference","c-formula","c-thickness"]}],
