    stem: "The sketch shows a semi-detached house with a storeroom in the rear garden. The owners wish to undertake an eco-refurbishment of the storeroom to make it suitable for use as a home office.",
    questionText: "A survey of the storeroom reveals: walls: random rubble, unrendered, 450 mm thick; roof: uninsulated, traditional cut roof with natural slate; floor: stone flags on earth. Select any two areas from the above and, using notes and freehand sketches, show the design detailing necessary to upgrade the storeroom to make it suitable for use as a home office. The refurbishment should be eco-friendly and should respect the character and appearance of the original storeroom. Justify your design choices.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 40,
    rows: [
    { id: "areas", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Design detailing to upgrade storeroom - 2 areas", marks: 32, contextNote: "Any two of the three printed areas, each notes 8 and sketches 8 = 16. Upgrading walls: a breathable structure letting moisture move out; hygroscopic, natural insulation such as hemp-lime, wood fibre or sheep’s wool; layers more permeable towards the outside; raking out and repointing in lime by hand; three coats of lime plaster. Upgrading roof: all members vented; slates removed, numbered and stored; decayed rafters cut back or replaced in treated timber of the same section; a vapour-diffuse membrane and counter battens; matching salvaged slates; cast-iron rainwater goods. Upgrading floor: flags photographed, numbered and lifted; earth replaced with compacted hardcore, blinding and a radon barrier; a hemp-lime or insulated slab; the flags relaid on lime or proprietary screed and sealed.", group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":16,"options":["Upgrading walls","Upgrading roof","Upgrading floor"]} },
    { id: "justification-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Justification for design choices - area 1", marks: 4, contextNote: "The choices for the first area justified, such as breathability and respect for the original character.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4] },
    { id: "justification-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Justification for design choices - area 2", marks: 4, contextNote: "The choices for the second area justified.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3,4] },
    ],
